governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The only failure is in my own acceptance test. It assumed list() hides completed todos by default, which the request never asked for, so the test was guessing at behaviour. I'm replacing it with one that checks only the rename. I'm also asking the commands owner to make sure no use of `done` slipped past the type checker and that list() keeps whatever default behaviour its existing tests specify.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The type checker and tests pass (13/13). Todo now uses `completed` in types, format, storage and commands. Round 2 checked commands for leftover uses of the old name that the type checker can't see. The acceptance test confirms add, complete and list use the new field. includeDone keeps its name because the request only covers Todo.done.)

